Mugunthan and all,

One more quick follow-up:

With that patch applied and us removing the SMSC LAN8710 PHY driver fro=
m the kernel and just using the default "unknown" driver, things are *m=
uch* better.=A0 (I have no idea why that PHY driver would be hurting us=
 since that is the exact PHY the TAM-3517 uses, but I'll take better pe=
rformance any day.)=A0 On average we're seeing 40 - 60Mbps in the trans=
mit direction and continuing to see the full ~95Mbps in the receive dir=
ection.=A0 We do still see some timeouts when transmitting, but they ar=
e certainly fewer and farther between.

There is one additional step that I can take which appears to=A0 comple=
tely fix our performance.=A0 Oddly, it's turning on our custom applicat=
ion!=A0 With our custom app running, suddenly we can do 95Mbps is *both=
* directions without any drops!=A0 Since our app in its idle state is r=
eally not doing anything but periodically reading and writing on all 4 =
AM3517 UARTs + periodically blipping out a one-way UDP status packet or=
 two + doing a little bit of stuff on the GPMC (we have a GPMC-based UA=
RT as well), there is _nothing_ there that seems like it should double-=
up our EMAC's transmit performance.=A0 If anything, I would have expect=
ed the unnecessary load to hurt us.

My theory at the moment is that this code is somehow keeping the EMAC f=
rom entering some form of a sleep or lower power state; and this someth=
ing must be different than whatever iperf is doing.=A0 (iperf chews up =
about 25% of the CPU by the way, so I don't think it's a general CPU st=
ress thing.)=A0 I know there are several power domains and such on this=
 chip, and I've seen lots of effort going into getting all of them to w=
ork properly over the past year.=A0 For our older 3.5-rc4 kernel, I've =
turned all power control stuff OFF.=A0 Our application does not require=
 low power features, so I've long considered that something to do when =
I have idle time on my hands.

Do you agree that this app holding something up seems like a good theor=
y?=A0 If so, what could possibly be shutting off or causing a pause tha=
t this custom app I've mentioned may be inadvertently keeping awake?=A0=
 We are already running our kernel with the "nohlt" option and the kern=
el configuration shown below.=A0 Is there anything else anyone would re=
commend we try?

Thanks!

